#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:532
msgid "Carpentry in the US still speaks feet and inches, including fractional inches. Metric-trained woodworkers converting plans must decide whether to soft-convert (nearest convenient millimetre) or hard-convert (exact 25.4 mm per inch) based on fit-critical parts."
msgstr "ABD'de marangozluk, kesirli inçler de dahil olmak üzere hâlâ fit ve inç konuşuyor. Metrik eğitimli ahşap işçileri dönüştürme planlarına uyum açısından kritik parçalara göre yumuşak dönüştürme (uygun en yakın milimetre) veya sert dönüştürme (inç başına tam 25,4 mm) arasında karar vermelidir."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2001
msgid "Carpet and flooring are sold by area—square metres or square feet—not by a single length. The reliable workflow is: measure length and width in one unit → multiply for area → convert area if the seller uses another unit → add waste → round up to pack coverage."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1989
msgid "Carpet Area Calculator Workflow"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1622
msgid "Carriers care about two constraints: how heavy a parcel is, and how much space it occupies on a truck or aircraft. Actual (scale) weight is what a calibrated scale reads in kilograms or pounds. Dimensional weight—also called volumetric weight—is a billing weight computed from the package’s outer dimensions using the carrier’s divisor formula."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1556
msgid "Carry-on limits are often lower and sometimes stated only in kilograms. Soft bags compress; hard cases do not. Weigh the packed bag, not the empty shell plus a guess. If you own a scale in pounds only, convert the limit first, write both numbers on a sticky note in the bag, and re-check after last-minute additions (duty-free bottles are a classic overage)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1387
msgid "Carryover cooking means food temperature rises after removal. Unit conversion does not change that physics; timing and resting still matter."
msgstr "Taşınarak pişirme, gıdanın çıkarıldıktan sonra sıcaklığının artması anlamına gelir. Birim dönüşümü bu fiziği değiştirmez; zamanlama ve dinlenme hala önemlidir."

